{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"e7f88a0478109251c89ae03c","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260815205750.169336-1-ebiggers%40kernel.org/","channels":["lkml"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260815205750.169336-1-ebiggers@kernel.org","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260815205750.169336-1-ebiggers%40kernel.org/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260815205750.169336-1-ebiggers@kernel.org"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 0/6] x86: add missing vzeroupper instructions","messages":{"20260816161450.05fd24f2@pumpkin":{"id":"20260816161450.05fd24f2@pumpkin","messageId":"20260816161450.05fd24f2@pumpkin","references":["20260815205750.169336-1-ebiggers@kernel.org"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260815205750.169336-1-ebiggers@kernel.org"],"author":{"name":"David Laight","address":"david.laight.linux@gmail.com"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Eric Biggers","address":"ebiggers@kernel.org"}],"cc":[{"name":"","address":"x86@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-raid@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Christoph Hellwig","address":"hch@infradead.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-crypto@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Herbert Xu","address":"herbert@gondor.apana.org.au"},{"name":"Taehee Yoo","address":"ap420073@gmail.com"},{"name":"","address":"netfilter-devel@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"Pablo Neira Ayuso","address":"pablo@netfilter.org"},{"name":"Florian Westphal","address":"fw@strlen.de"},{"name":"Phil Sutter","address":"phil@nwl.cc"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T15:14:50.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T15:14:50.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH 0/6] x86: add missing vzeroupper instructions","mailingLists":[{"id":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"linux-kernel.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Sat, 15 Aug 2026 13:57:44 -0700\nEric Biggers <ebiggers@kernel.org> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"Assembly code using YMM or ZMM registers is supposed to end with the"},{"depth":1,"text":"vzeroupper instruction in order to avoid degrading the performance of"},{"depth":1,"text":"any later SSE code.  Since this only affects performance and not"},{"depth":1,"text":"correctness, it is sometimes overlooked.  Most kernel code does it"},{"depth":1,"text":"correctly, but a few cases were missed.  This series fixes them."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"It should be easiest to take the full series through the x86 tree."}],"lineCount":7,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Would it be better to an an unconditional vzeroupper in kernel_fpu_end()?\nIt could go in kernel_fpu_start() but that might have a bigger effect\non latency.\n(I assume there is one in kernel_fpu_start() if it actually saves\nthe user registers?)"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Looking the latency/uops seems reasonably on everything 'recent' except\nzen-1 and knights-landing.\nAlthough the microcode patch for zen-2 might make that a lot worse."},{"kind":"code","text":"\tDavid  "},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Eric Biggers (6):"},{"depth":1,"text":"  xor: add missing vzeroupper to AVX code"},{"depth":1,"text":"  raid6: add missing vzeroupper to AVX2 code"},{"depth":1,"text":"  raid6: add missing vzeroupper to AVX-512 code"},{"depth":1,"text":"  crypto: x86/aria - add missing vzeroupper in AVX2 code"},{"depth":1,"text":"  crypto: x86/aria - add missing vzeroupper in AVX-512 code"},{"depth":1,"text":"  netfilter: nft_set_pipapo_avx2: add missing vzeroupper"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" arch/x86/crypto/aria-aesni-avx2-asm_64.S  |  6 ++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" arch/x86/crypto/aria-gfni-avx512-asm_64.S |  3 +++"},{"depth":1,"text":" lib/raid/raid6/x86/avx2.c                 |  6 ++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" lib/raid/raid6/x86/avx512.c               |  6 ++++++"},{"depth":1,"text":" lib/raid/raid6/x86/recov_avx2.c           |  2 ++"},{"depth":1,"text":" lib/raid/raid6/x86/recov_avx512.c         |  2 ++"},{"depth":1,"text":" lib/raid/xor/x86/xor-avx.c                |  1 +"},{"depth":1,"text":" net/netfilter/nft_set_pipapo_avx2.c       | 17 ++++++++---------"},{"depth":1,"text":" 8 files changed, 34 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"base-commit: db2ddb87143519e20a95aa36c60b36107b736a58"}],"lineCount":21,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260815205750.169336-1-ebiggers@kernel.org"}},"rootIds":["20260816161450.05fd24f2@pumpkin"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["20260816161450.05fd24f2@pumpkin"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}